          #EnoughInjectives.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              One says that a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              %strong enough injectives
              if every object admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              into an injective object.
          %p
            (The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} dual
            notion is that of a
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
          %p
            Assuming the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of injective objects is injective.
          .num_remark
