                holds.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The implications “1.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              2.”, “3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              4.”, “3.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              1.”, and “4.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              2.” are trivial.
            %p
              The equivalence “3.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇔
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leftrightarrow
              5.” follows directly from the interpretation rules of the stack semantics.
            %p
              The implication “2.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              4.” employs the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change#GeometricMorphism"} extra left-adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! : \mathcal{E}/A \to \mathcal{E}
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
