              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flabby+sheaf"} flabby
              (this is particularly easy using the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The analogs of Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfInternalNotionsOfInjectivity"}
              and Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfInternalAndExternalInjectivity"}
              for abelian group objects instead of unstructured objects hold as well, with mostly the same proofs. Condition 1. then refers to the functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ab
