                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-, X] : Ab(\mathcal{E})^op \to Ab(\mathcal{E})
          %h3#topological_spaces Topological spaces
          %p
            In the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of all topological spaces, the injective objects are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indiscrete+spaces"} indiscrete spaces
          %p
            In the category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            spaces (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
          %p In the above two cases, this refers to injectivity with respect to monomorphisms.
          %p
            In the category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            spaces, the injective objects with respect to homeomorphic embeddings are precisely those given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+topologies"} Scott topologies
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+lattices"} continuous lattices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            these are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locale"} spatial
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em injective spaces
          %p
            In the category of all spaces, the injectives with respect to homeomorphic embeddings (i.e.,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            reflections are continuous lattices under the Scott topology.
          %h3#boolean_algebras Boolean algebras
          %p
            Injective objects in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebras"} Boolean algebras
            are precisely the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Boolean+algebras"} complete Boolean algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+objects"} projective objects
            in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+spaces"} Stone spaces
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremally+disconnected+topological+space"} extremally disconnected
            ones (the closure of every open set is again open).
          %h3#posets Posets
          %p
            In the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            and order-preserving functions, the singleton is the only poset which satisfies the extension property along all monomorphisms. However, if we require injectives to satisfy the extension property only with respect to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattices"} complete lattices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is an injective poset and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            to get a new poset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
